  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of health, protection and PSS assistance to refugees that fled Ukraine, through a health team and PSS/protection capacity building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Main goal is to reduce health and protection risks for refugees and Third Country Nationals, by ensuring access to quality essential lifesaving and high-impact health care services and access to quality protection and improved PSS services, with a specific focus on the most vulnerable. The project contains 2 major components:1)Provision of primary health services in Tudora and Palanca border crossing points and Palanca bus transit center and health promotion activities .2)Capacity building of MHPSS program with special attention towards PSS for the war-affected population and integration of comprehensive protection services.</narrative>
  </description>
